              "id": "c",
              "text": "It stays the same until the end"
            },
            {
              "id": "d",
              "text": "It roughly doubles"
            }
          ],
          "answer_id": "b",
          "explanation": "Discarding the impossible half leaves an interval about half as long, which is why the search shrinks so fast.",
          "scene_id": "s3"
        },
        {
          "prompt": "If you double the number of sorted elements n, how does the worst-case number of comparisons for binary search change?",
